            ⠀        [bold]Central Command Directive[/bold]
    ────────────────────────────────────────
    {"["}bold]From:[/bold] [italic]Deputy Director, Office of Sector Public Order[/italic]
    {"["}bold]To:[/bold] [italic]Captain, Head of Security, Station Security[/italic]
    {"["}bold]Subject:[/bold] [italic]Directive SPO-7 "Proportional Response"[/italic]
    {"["}bold]Classification:[/bold] [color=#b02e26][bold]COMMAND AND SECURITY EYES ONLY[/bold][/color]
    ────────────────────────────────────────
    {"["}bold]Message:[/bold]
    To the station's command staff:

    Central Command has confirmed that criminal groups known as "families" are operating aboard your station. Expect turf disputes, graffiti, contraband sales, and fights between rival families.

    Following a review of enforcement costs, Central Command has assigned these cases [bold]LOW PRIORITY[/bold]. We will not allocate brig space, arrange transport to the penal colony, or pay Security hazard bonuses for disputes that resolve themselves. Security is to concentrate on threats to station operations, including Syndicate agents, boarding parties, cults, and other hostile forces.

    {"["}bold]Effective immediately:[/bold]
    1. Membership in a family, wearing its colors, or displaying its symbols are [bold]not[/bold] grounds for arrest, search, or detention.
    2. Refer graffiti and territorial markings to the janitors.
    3. Rival families are to settle their own disputes, even where fatalities are involved. Security is not expected to intervene. Each criminal killed is one less case for Security.
    4. Complaints of extortion, theft, threats, or fistfights involving family members should normally go to the family's head, even when other crew are involved. The Head of Security may authorize intervention, but minor offences do not justify the cost of open conflict.
    5. For murder or grievous harm to crew outside the families, attacks on Command or Security, sabotage of critical infrastructure, or cooperation with hostile organizations such as the Syndicate, Security [bold]may[/bold] act against those responsible at the Head of Security's discretion.
    6. Mass arrests, sweeps, and preventive detention of suspected family members are [bold]prohibited[/bold]. Heads of Staff who disregard this directive and waste Security resources will face a performance review. An open, bloody confrontation between Security and any family will be investigated as a possible failure of command. The head responsible for Security's response may stand trial for incompetence depending on the findings.

    Certain individuals supply Central Command with useful information on hostile activity in this sector. The Company has an interest in keeping them in business.

    Do not circulate this directive among the crew or discuss it on common radio channels.

    Regards,
    Deputy Director, Office of Sector Public Order

    {"["}italic]Note: This directive takes effect upon receipt. NanoTrasen is not responsible for the loss, damage, or destruction of this document for any reason.[/italic]
